                    {
                        "translation_id": "3b203f07-1992-4083-9eb6-bb0097024854",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb683345-ef5d-38ad-9b60-bb5061ab7444",
                        "source_sense_id": "6b9da1e6-f55b-3fc2-bbb3-92d34b01a63c",
                        "source_sense_description": "größere wissenschaftliche Abhandlung über ein bestimmtes Thema",
                        "target_lang_word": "monograph",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "monograph",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "56399133-467f-32d7-b016-1f7cd54e7b44",
                                        "entry_id": "5fa0b178-3c50-37fb-abd0-e76f4fa843b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A scholarly book or a treatise on a single subject or a group of related subjects, usually written by one person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d225d576-55e4-43de-9906-3a70ba2666a7",
                                                "sense_id": "56399133-467f-32d7-b016-1f7cd54e7b44",
                                                "text": "It may still be years before we see, what we all look forward to, the great and final book on Knossos. Meanwhile learned monographs on different sections of the subject have been fast accumulating. They form the principal contents of six successive Annuals of the British School at Athens, and a not inconsiderable portion of the six corresponding volumes of The Journal of Hellenic Studies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "457d241c-1595-4725-b733-3caeb44a787d",
                                                "sense_id": "56399133-467f-32d7-b016-1f7cd54e7b44",
                                                "text": "The complex history of the Wirral Railway and the lines with which it was interlinked needs more lucid treatment than is given in this 39-page monograph - and clearer maps and an index."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df408b87-d967-4eec-bab9-5bf7dd7168ff",
                                                "sense_id": "56399133-467f-32d7-b016-1f7cd54e7b44",
                                                "text": "1996 March, Cullen Murphy, \"Hello Darkness\", The Atlantic Monthly, Volume 277, No. 3, pp. 22-24.\nI had never given much thought to the role of darkness in ordinary human affairs until I read a monograph prepared by John Staudenmaier, a historian of technology and a Jesuit priest, for a recent conference at MIT."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35fc536b-7ba4-4191-9711-99753dac9d64",
                                                "sense_id": "56399133-467f-32d7-b016-1f7cd54e7b44",
                                                "text": "Crooke made a few references to two of his monographs (1896a and 1896b) but did not take quotations from his own works."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c164d5b0-2423-3f72-9f8a-c566b8b25a20",
                                        "entry_id": "5fa0b178-3c50-37fb-abd0-e76f4fa843b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A single letter, especially one which represents a phoneme by itself when held in contrast to letters within polygraphs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncommon"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "monograph",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f38839e5-4883-3b08-9f87-d519be88c243",
                                        "entry_id": "e70f4cdd-b0e4-3388-b124-ad7bcf05fc4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To write a monograph on (a subject)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7584927c-3381-43a5-b1ad-95e978642ab1",
                                                "sense_id": "f38839e5-4883-3b08-9f87-d519be88c243",
                                                "text": "It is among the most studied, monographed, celebrated and sent-up works of modern art, and perhaps as influential as any from the last century."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb14fb97-e67b-3a26-98fb-a86c3a513d4a",
                                        "entry_id": "e70f4cdd-b0e4-3388-b124-ad7bcf05fc4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the FDA: to publish a standard that authorizes the use of (a substance)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7e3e798b-d5e0-42f5-a52b-031c281b32b5",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb683345-ef5d-38ad-9b60-bb5061ab7444",
                        "source_sense_id": "6b9da1e6-f55b-3fc2-bbb3-92d34b01a63c",
                        "source_sense_description": "größere wissenschaftliche Abhandlung über ein bestimmtes Thema",
                        "target_lang_word": "treatise",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "treatise",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cfd041bb-6b6f-3855-b9e5-2462f257bd6a",
                                        "entry_id": "d3c8325a-eab4-3f85-956f-fc1c3d8e90ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A formal, usually lengthy, systematic discourse on some subject."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af839381-6400-46db-812a-e479e5fc5fa3",
                                                "sense_id": "cfd041bb-6b6f-3855-b9e5-2462f257bd6a",
                                                "text": "\"As you cannot make a speech, you must,\" said Henrietta, \"put it into a treatise.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae2baa6e-bc7e-4aa7-9eac-8c282b9331c9",
                                                "sense_id": "cfd041bb-6b6f-3855-b9e5-2462f257bd6a",
                                                "text": "“[…] We are engaged in a great work, a treatise on our river fortifications, perhaps ? But since when did army officers afford the luxury of amanuenses in this simple republic ?[…]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4a4b6d1-22f4-4c5c-ad7f-3abda53ea347",
                                                "sense_id": "cfd041bb-6b6f-3855-b9e5-2462f257bd6a",
                                                "text": "And if someone wants to know how to make objections to actual craftsmen themselves on the subject of art in general or any particular art, there are published treatises available, as you know."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "703139a5-11a9-421b-95df-03d8559c2466",
                                                "sense_id": "cfd041bb-6b6f-3855-b9e5-2462f257bd6a",
                                                "text": "Some poems, echoing the purpose of early poetic treatises on scientific principles, attempt to elucidate the mathematical concepts that underlie prime numbers. Others play with primes’ cultural associations. Still others derive their structure from mathematical patterns involving primes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f2aa67e2-628a-492d-b18a-64ac32607d5b",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb683345-ef5d-38ad-9b60-bb5061ab7444",
